<%#
# One choice of a group of radio buttons, with what it asks for under it

A card with a radio button, a title and a one-line hint. What the choice needs (a select, two fields, a password) goes in the block (an
empty block when it needs nothing) and is shown only while the choice is the chosen one: the script of the shell switches the
bodies when a radio button changes, for the cards that sit in a container with `data-choice-group`. A disabled choice cannot be
chosen (and says why in its hint).

## Local variables:

- `name`: the name of the radio buttons (`organization[mode]`).
- `value`: what this choice sends.
- `checked`: whether it is the chosen one.
- `title`, `hint`: the text of the card.
- `disabled` (optional): the choice cannot be chosen.
%>
<% disabled = local_assigns.fetch(:disabled, false) %>
<% body = yield %>
<div class="admin-choice<%= ' admin-choice--disabled' if disabled %>" data-choice="<%= value %>">
  <label class="admin-choice__head">
    <%= radio_button_tag name, value, checked, disabled: disabled %>
    <span class="admin-choice__text">
      <span class="admin-choice__title"><%= title %></span>
      <span class="admin-choice__hint"><%= hint %></span>
    </span>
  </label>
  <% if body.present? %>
    <div class="admin-choice__body" data-choice-body <%= 'hidden' unless checked %>>
      <%= body %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
